    "summary": "A single hand-woven specimen strip for a Kente cloth, made of imported European dark blue and white cotton. The warp is of white cotton, along which run a few narrow stripes of dark blue cotton. A pattern is formed in the weft of pairs of blue bands using a second pair of heddles that flank patterns of lines and shapes built of continuous and discontinuous supplementary weft which cross the strip at regular intervals. These patterns are denser at the two ends. The ends form a loose fringe",
